## How it works

### The head is the authority

The notebook's own \`<head>\` holds the card metadata — \`<title>\`, \`description\`, \`og:title\`, \`og:description\`, \`og:image\`, and \`og:video\` + \`og:video:type\` when there is a video. The atproto records are a mirror of it, not a second opinion.

Publishing writes the edited title, description and poster URL **into** the head first, then reads them back out and fills the records from what it read (\`headMeta.write\` then \`headMeta.read\`). There is no path where a record carries a value the head does not. Two heads to patch, one code path each:

- **this runtime** — \`document.head\` is patched in place. That is the head [\`@tomlarkworthy/exporter-3\`](https://tomlarkworthy.github.io/lopecode/notebooks/@tomlarkworthy_exporter-3.html) scans on export, so every later export and save-in-place carries the values. \`og:video\`/\`og:video:type\` are not in exporter-3's managed set, so they survive as preserved metas; \`og:image\` and \`og:description\` are managed and re-emitted from the same values.
- **a dropped or forked file** — the parsed document is patched before it is serialised.

Earlier the widget's title and description fields only *prefilled* from the head and the edited value went to the record, which made the form the authority and let the file drift from what the feed showed.

### Posters and video: \`com.lopecode.media\`

A poster is not a bundle file and not an inline \`data:\` URL. It is a \`com.lopecode.media\` record — a required \`poster\` blob (\`image/*\`, ≤ 1 MB), an optional \`video\` blob (\`video/*\`, ≤ 5 MB), plus \`alt\`, \`width\`, \`height\`, \`sourceId\`, \`createdAt\` — served by the media proxy at:

\`\`\`
poster  https://images.lopecode.com/{did}/{rkey}
video   https://images.lopecode.com/{did}/{rkey}/video
\`\`\`

**The rkey IS the poster blob's CID.** Two things follow. The URL is known as soon as the bytes are, so \`publishMedia()\` can be called on its own, before any bundle publish — which is what makes the URL exist in time to be written into the head. And the URL is a serialised blob ref: given one, \`getRecord\` returns the blob objects to reuse verbatim for \`bundle.coverImage\`, \`site.standard.document.coverImage\` and the Bluesky \`embed.external.thumb\` — no re-upload, no CORS fetch of the image.

The widget offers two poster sources: upload a file, or pick an image block already inside the notebook being published (any \`<script data-mime="image/*">\`, with \`sourceId\` set to that block's id). Generating a poster by screenshotting the DOM was dropped — it handles complex DOM badly.

An \`og:image\` that is some other absolute URL (the legacy GitHub Pages ones, or a \`data:\` URL) is still fetched by \`resolveImageBytes\` and uploaded, and a media record is created for it, so the head converges on a proxy URL. A fetch that fails (CORS) leaves the original \`og:image\` in the head and the records without a cover.

### What one publish writes

| record | rkey | when |
|---|---|---|
| \`com.lopecode.media\` | the poster blob's CID | whenever a poster resolves; skipped when \`og:image\` already names one and no video was added |
| \`site.standard.publication\` | TID | once per author; upserted, and skipped when nothing changed |
| \`site.standard.document\` | TID | every publish; \`putRecord\` in place when the bundle carries \`stdDocUri\` |
| \`app.bsky.feed.post\` | TID | only when **Share to Bluesky** is ticked |
| \`com.lopecode.bundle\` | \`slugifyTitle(title)\` | every publish, written last |
| \`com.lopecode.bundle.version\` | \`{bundleRkey}--{TID}\` | on republish: a verbatim snapshot of the bundle about to be overwritten |

The document is written twice when Share is on. The post's \`embed.external.associatedRefs\` strong-ref the document and the publication, and the document's \`bskyPostRef\` strong-refs the post; the cycle only resolves by writing the document, then the post, then the document again at the same TID. \`publishedAt\` is read back off the live record and preserved across both writes, so an update does not bump the doc to the top of an indexer's feed; \`updatedAt\` is stamped on every in-place rewrite.

The bundle is written last because it is the only record of truth for the sidecar URIs — \`bskyPostUri\` and \`stdDocUri\` live there and nowhere else. A republish that does not rewrite a sidecar (Share left off, or the standard.site step failed and degraded to a warning) carries the prior bundle's URI forward instead of dropping it. \`com.lopecode.bundle.crossRef\` was the earlier home for the Bluesky URI; it is retired, and \`adoptLegacyCrossRefs()\` moves what those records hold onto the bundle and deletes them.

### Lexicon: \`com.lopecode.bundle\`

A record at \`at://{did}/com.lopecode.bundle/{rkey}\`. One record per published snapshot. \`rkey\` is derived from the title via \`utils.slugifyTitle\`, so two publishes under the same title overwrite each other (the prior value is snapshotted into \`com.lopecode.bundle.version\` first).

| field | type | meaning |
|---------------|----------|---------|
| \`$type\` | string | always \`"com.lopecode.bundle"\` |
| \`title\` | string | human title |
| \`files\` | array | one entry per \`<script id data-mime>\` block |
| \`createdAt\` | datetime | ISO 8601 |
| \`description\` | string? | mirror of \`og:description\`, read back off the head |
| \`coverImage\` | blob? | the \`poster\` blob of the \`com.lopecode.media\` record \`og:image\` names — a standalone PDS blob, not a bundle file |
| \`bskyPostUri\` | string? | the companion \`app.bsky.feed.post\` |
| \`stdDocUri\` | string? | the \`site.standard.document\` |

Each \`files[]\` entry:

| field       | type   | meaning |
|-------------|--------|---------|
| \`id\`      | string | script tag id, e.g. \`@user/module\`, \`@user/module/asset.png\`, \`bootconf.json\` |
| \`encoding\`| string | \`"text"\` or \`"base64"\` from \`data-encoding\` |
| \`blob\`    | blob   | atproto blob ref — carries CID (v1 raw + sha-256), \`mimeType\`, \`size\` |

### Pipeline

1. **Source**: \`exportToHTML\` from \`@tomlarkworthy/exporter-3\` serializes the running runtime, *or* \`file.text()\` reads a dropped \`.html\` lopebook. The head is read once here to prefill the title, description, poster and video fields.
2. \`DOMParser\` extracts every \`<script id data-mime>\` block.
3. Compute CID v1 (raw codec, sha-256) per block client-side.
4. Diff against the per-DID set of CIDs cached in \`localStorage\`; the dialog renders \`NEW\` vs \`CACHED\` for each block before you click Publish.
5. On Publish: resolve the poster to a \`com.lopecode.media\` record, write title/description/\`og:image\`/\`og:video\` into the head, and read the head back. Everything below uses what was read.
6. \`uploadBlob\` only the new blocks. The bundle and its version snapshot are written in one \`applyWrites\`, so a snapshot can never be missing for a record that was overwritten. The CID cache in \`localStorage\` is **only persisted after that write succeeds** — otherwise an orphaned blob (uploaded, never referenced, then GC'd by the PDS) would leave the cache claiming success forever.
7. If the write returns \`BlobNotFound\` (cache thought a blob existed but the PDS had GC'd it), \`at-write\` clears the cache for this publish, re-uploads every block, and retries once.
8. Fire-and-forget \`POST https://contrail.lopecode.com/xrpc/com.lopecode.notifyOfUpdate\` so the contrail indexer picks up the new bundle without waiting for the next jetstream poll.

A first publish uploads every block (~80 for a typical notebook). Subsequent publishes touching one module upload one or two.

### Scopes

Sign-in asks for \`atproto repo:com.lopecode.bundle repo:com.lopecode.bundle.version blob:*/*\` — enough to publish, snapshot and delete bundles, nothing else. Publishing upgrades the session in place via \`ensureScopes\`, once and up front so one popup covers the whole publish, adding \`repo:com.lopecode.media\`, \`repo:site.standard.publication\` and \`repo:site.standard.document\`, plus \`repo:app.bsky.feed.post\` when Share is ticked. A declined or broken upgrade does not abort the publish: the bundle and snapshot need only scopes already held, so they still land and the result card names what was skipped.

### Deleting

