const _spec_6_0 = function _anonymous(md) {return (md`Four things fail today.

**Credentials live in the tab.** \`@tomlarkworthy/at-login\` is a browser client: its own prose says "Tokens stored locally; DPoP key is non-extractable in IndexedDB". A second device signs in again, and a public atproto client's session is limited to 2 weeks against 180-day refresh tokens for a confidential one ([atproto OAuth spec](https://atproto.com/specs/oauth), read 2026-10-04). API keys for other services are pasted per notebook.

**Pairing needs a local port.** An https page reaching \`ws://127.0.0.1\` is gated behind the Local Network Access prompt since Chrome 151, and headless Chrome refuses it even with the permission granted (\`verify-https-pairing.mjs\`, recorded 2026-08-04). A phone cannot pair with a laptop's Claude Code at all.

**Nothing reaches a notebook from outside.** A tab cannot receive a webhook, and a hidden tab does not recompute (seen 2026-10-04 and again on 2026-10-05, when this spec's own tab stopped applying edits). A message sent while the tab is closed has nowhere to wait.

