Tom, 2026-10-04, on the interpreter: "I would not rule out QuickJS yet because it seems hard to see how an agent will be able to self modify on demand without it." It is the only option that evaluates a string inside the running isolate without a restart and without the Paid plan. Tom's Brain is on Workers Paid ("I have the $5 per month"), so Dynamic Workers are available to it.

**A Durable Object as the runtime** (Tom: "maybe a runtime needs to be a durable function so the runtime state persists across requests"). A plain Worker has many short-lived isolates; a cell's value in one is not seen by the next request. One Durable Object is one instance whose memory lasts between requests, so one runtime there has one set of cell values, as a tab does. Costs: memory is lost on eviction and on every deploy, so a cell that must keep its value reads it from SQLite on boot (the \`sticky\` pattern, server side); all requests pass through one object in one region; it is billed while awake. Proposed, not decided: the dataplane's runtime lives in its Durable Object, and a route can opt out to the stateless path for bulk reads.

**A self-upgrade loses memory and keeps storage.** For an agent that deploys its own change: write the transcript and the next intended step to SQLite, set an alarm, ask the guard to deploy. The new version wakes on the alarm and continues. If the new version fails its health check the guard puts the old one back, which wakes on the same alarm and finds the checkpoint. Not observed.

**For the export.** For a Worker to change itself it needs its own source, which \`toString()\` on a running module does not give back in full. The export would carry each module's source as a text part beside the compiled one, making the Worker self-serialising in the sense a lopecode notebook is.

**Limits on the agent, whichever mechanism.** A sender allowlist checked before anything reaches the model; no deploy tool until the edit loop is proven; a daily spend cap as \`openrouter-gateway\` has; the key is an API key, since a Claude subscription login does not work server-side. The kernel makes no model call. A chat service is one more dataplane module with a route: verify, parse, send. WhatsApp needs a Meta business app and a registered number and limits free-form replies to 24 hours after the user's last message (from memory, not checked).`);};
