md`### Adding a chat

\`robocoop5(options)\` returns a chat. The chat above is \`robocoop5({ settings: true, invalidation })\`. Another notebook imports it and passes what differs:

\`\`\`js
import {robocoop5, defaultWatches} from "@tomlarkworthy/robocoop-5"

reviewer = robocoop5({
  group: "reviews",          // sessions save as @reviews/<id>; default "robocoop5-session"
  model: "openai/gpt-5",     // a value, or a function read every step; default: the settings panel
  system: "Review only.",    // the same
  tools: ts => ts.filter(t => !/write|edit|eval|python/.test(t.id)),
  hooks: {
    beforeTool: ({ name, args }) => null,       // return a string to refuse the call with that reason
    afterTool: ({ name, args, result }) => {},  // return a replacement result
    beforeComplete: info => null                // return a string to reject task_complete; info.summary is its text
  },
  height: 500,               // px or a CSS length ("80vh"); default 600. Drag the bottom edge to resize
  persist: true,             // save every session as a main (goes into the file on the next save);
                             // default false: a "save" checkbox per session
  settings: false,           // key / model / prompt panel; one chat per page can host it
  watches: () => [...defaultWatches(), { label: "rows", read: () => rows }],
                             // values the agent is told about each step: in full on the first step, then
                             // only what changed. Default: the module list and every erroring cell
  invalidation               // detaches the chat's listeners when the cell re-runs
})
\`\`\`

Every chat lists every session on the page. Writes into a saved session module, or into robocoop-5, are refused whatever the hooks say. That limits the model, not the page: \`eval_js\` and \`run_python\` run arbitrary code, so drop them from \`tools\` to confine an agent.

A re-run cell shows the session it was showing, found by \`group\`. The cells below it hold state shared by every chat on the page.`
