const _doc_hook_turnEnd = function _doc_hook_turnEnd(md){return(
md`### \`hook_turnEnd\`
Runs when the model stopped, or replied with something the loop cannot run. \`ctx.kind\` says which:

| kind | what happened | a rule may return |
|---|---|---|
| \`complete\` | the completion tool was called on its own | \`{continue: text}\`: the call is refused with that text |
| \`batched\` | the completion tool was called beside other tools | \`{continue: text}\` |
| \`stall\` | a reply with no tool call (\`finishReason\` is \`stop\` or \`length\`) | \`{continue: text}\` sent as a system message, or \`{end: true}\` |
| \`truncated\` | a tool call whose arguments do not parse | \`{continue: text}\`, the tool result |
| \`malformed\` | the provider rejected the model's own call and returned nothing | \`{retry: text}\` |
| \`images_dropped\` | a text-only model refused a request holding images; they were removed | \`{retry: text}\` |

The first non-null result wins; null lets the turn end. The loop, not the rule, bounds how often a turn
can be continued: once per turn for \`complete\` and for \`batched\`, \`stallNudgeLimit\` consecutive
stalls, \`malformedRetryLimit\` retries.`
)};
